// Astro half of the parity fixture. Its Svelte twin is ./fixture.svelte and the
// two must emit the same contract markup; parity.test.ts is what says so.
//
// Deliberately trivial and deliberately NOT a real element: it exercises the
// harness (compile both, render both, normalise both, diff) while ui/svelte and
// ui/astro are still empty, so the day the first real adapter pair lands the
// only new thing is the element. It also pins the four normalisations the
// diff needs, one per shape the two frameworks disagree on: a boolean attribute
// (data-fixture), an interpolated text node, a static class, and whitespace.
const { text = 'hello' } = Astro.props;
---

<p class="bb-fixture" data-fixture>{text}</p>
